# Confluence diagrams

Pair this plugin with **`drawio-author`** / **`drawio-repair`** from the
`nodadyoushutup-drawio` plugin. Do not invent a second diagram craft here.

## When

The user asks for a figure on a Confluence page, or the page’s Overview /
sections clearly need an architecture, workflow, or dependency graph.

## Procedure

1. **Author locally** — write or repair a `.drawio` under the repo’s docs (or
   an agreed path) with `drawio-author` / `drawio-repair`. Honor the layout
   contract (lanes, gaps, edge buses).
2. **Export for humans** — when the host expects a raster preview, also
   produce PNG/SVG from the same diagram if tooling is available; otherwise
   attach the `.drawio` and say so.
3. **Attach** — `confluence_upload_attachment` (or batch upload) onto the
   target page. Prefer a clear filename (`confluence-workflow.drawio`,
   `architecture.png`).
4. **Reference in body** — add a short H2 (for example `## Diagram`) with a
   one-line caption and, when the site supports it, the attachment link or
   draw.io macro the host already uses. Prefer
   `confluence_update_page_section` so the rest of the page stays intact.
5. **Do not** paste raw mxfile XML into the page body as a code fence.

## Repair

Broken layout on an existing attachment: download when needed, run
`drawio-repair`, re-upload (new version). Cursor “Assertion Failed” on open
is `drawio-editor` triage — not a Confluence content bug.

## Refuse

- Do not invent space/page just to host a diagram — create/update gates still
  apply (`atlassian-confluence-create` / `atlassian-confluence-update`).
- Do not replace an existing draw.io macro blob by guessing storage XML.
